KG42.register("clusters-038f2a6c6c5b2e89e9069c0a",{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v142-d-K004","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","label":"Price- and preference-driven EMTS automated trading","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K004","label":"Price- and preference-driven EMTS automated trading","market_meaning":"Participant EMTS uses market information, energy preferences, and price limits to form automated trading behavior and requires account access permission. The simple price-threshold purchase rule is only a general design example; the buy and sell limit orders at the BMG reporting stage are connected as shared interfaces. Trading retains a virtual-layer meaning, and parts between decision, submission, and transaction execution remain unclosed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["coordination","activation","bidding"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The simple EMTS threshold and demand-side management are general examples or possibilities and cannot be presumed to be the complete actual strategy of all BMG customers. Shared R002 and R003 connect only their reporting-stage order behavior, and the R003 feed-in tariff discussion retains its original conditions. An observed market price is not automatically equivalent to the clearing price subsequently formed by a given order.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"This cluster takes participant-side automated decision-making and order placement as the responsible activity and distinguishes it from market-side matching and clearing. The two formalizations of the same purchase example in R005 and R006 are retained as alternative expressions; this is not used to construct two purchases or additional causal steps, nor is automation elevated to a universal necessary condition for basic market operation.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide price-information response, simple purchase trigger, and price-signal design content."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplement the virtual trading boundary, participant preferences, and account access conditions; the purchase threshold and R005 are retained as alternative expressions of the same example."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Share only the EMTS demand order placement and the reporting-stage maximum price-limit behavior; the primary attribution is v142-d-K003."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Share only the EMTS supply order placement and the reporting-stage minimum price-limit behavior; the primary attribution is v142-d-K003."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"rationale":"The two expressions come from the same simple EMTS purchase example and are placed respectively in coordinated-decision and execution contexts. Both representations are retained, not counted as two independent purchase rules, and it is not thereby asserted that a cleared execution event necessarily follows the decision."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22"],"rationale":"The same BMG passage links the display of price and supply-demand information with automated trading that depends on participant preferences, supporting the complementarity of information response and trading conditions; it does not provide a new execution sequence or transaction guarantee."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"The preferences and account access required for automated trading form an operational interface with demand order submission through the EMTS; the specific maximum price-limit offer is limited to the reporting-stage strategy and is not derived from the general threshold example."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"Supply preferences and account access support the EMTS supply order placement interface. The simple purchase trigger has no corresponding sell expression, and a symmetric sell-threshold rule cannot be generated from it."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"rationale":"Both places use the local price function to carry the comparison condition of the same simple EMTS example; the node display representative does not merge variables, parameters, or edges of different functional endpoints."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O02","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"rationale":"The condition content comes from the same purchase example, but the local activity, index, and formalized source labels differ. They are associated as alternative expressions, neither deleting the original expression nor expanding it into a bidirectional condition."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O03","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x001","v141-c-R006::x::x_R006_buy"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"rationale":"Both represent the example purchase action, but one describes a decision with a participant index, while the other describes executing the decision upon activation. The original text does not distinguish two events or confirm variable identity, so they are retained as alternative expressions of the same kind."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O04","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta001","v141-c-R006::theta::theta_R006_p_local"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"rationale":"Both explain the market price in the same example, but the observation time point and activation time point are not independently defined. The two representations of the parameter are retained, without forcing them to share the same period identity."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O05","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta002","v141-c-R006::theta::theta_R006_p_max"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"rationale":"Both explain the maximum purchase price limit of the simple EMTS, but one has a participant index and the other is an unindexed example. Index instantiation has not been confirmed, and they are not rewritten as a unified parameter object."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G01","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The same purchase sentence is represented respectively as a coordinated decision and an execution decision; the source does not prove that they are two events, nor establish a correspondence between a cleared transaction and the threshold action. R005 is labeled equivalent_translation and R006 is labeled source, but the citation does not directly provide these symbols, binary domain, units, or indices; both sets of original objects remain frozen.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x001","v141-c-R006::x::x_R006_buy","v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E001","v141-c-R006::E::v141-c-R006-E001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should verify the semantics of the purchase action, the formalized source, and the participant and time indices. Before confirmation, retain the alternative expressions and the edges at different endpoints, do not add a decision-to-execution dependency, and do not supplement the behavior when the price reaches or exceeds the price limit."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The source mentions real-time supply-demand data, forecasting, and strategy formation, but the current chain does not cover how these inputs generate order electricity quantities, nor does it define the correspondence between the observed price and the next trading period. Preferences and account access alone cannot close the entire process from automated order placement to transaction.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e34"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Obtain source-grounded data inputs, forecast quantities, strategy, and time-period interfaces, and distinguish submission, allocation, and actual fund transfer; missing algorithms and state transitions continue to be explicitly left blank."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Participant-level EMTS and blockchain platforms do not yet have approved dedicated objects, and existing execution or coordination nodes cannot replace all responsibilities of these systems. The relevant proposal remains unapproved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R006::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g03-e005","v141-b-g03-e006"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-prop-emts","v141-b-g03-p01","proposal:v141-b-g01-information-system"],"required_work":"Manually review the EMTS and platform proposal and the scope of duplication, and then have C decide how system responsibilities and account access are expressed; the EMTS must not be directly equated with the local market operator."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The evidence for the simple strategy, automation conditions, and the BMG's actual order placement strategy has not been independently reviewed; the alternative-expression association is merely a model proposal awaiting checking.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g03-e020","v141-b-g03-e023"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the boundary between the example and actual implementation, the optionality of automation, and the meaning of virtual trading; retain the unverified status of all evidence."}]},"rule_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-9ca8822ee86e3e13","COMP-cca2f1628c10ac64","KG31-e2bea6d6e2936fab","KG40-12aedc3eec573697","KG40-20f45ec4bdcbac06"]});
